<h1>keyboard_get_numlock</h1>
<p>You can use this function to find the status of the keypad number lock with <b>true</b> being returned for on, and <b>false</b> returned for off.</p>
<p class="note"><b><span class="note">NOTE</span> </b>This functionality is only available in the Windows exe builds and will not function on any other device.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4><b>Syntax:</b></h4>
<p class="code">keyboard_get_numlock();</p>
<p> </p>
<h4><b>Returns:</b></h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Bool"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Boolean</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4><b>Example:</b></h4>
<p class="code">if (keyboard_get_numlock()) <br/>
{<br/>
    keyboard_set_numlock(false);<br/>
}<br/>
else<br/>
{<br/>
    keyboard_set_numlock(true);<br/>
}</p>
<p>The above example code will get the state of the numberlock key and if it is on (true) it will set it to off (false) and vice-versa.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
